  "goodToKnow": "Der Nationalismus is nationalism. Because of its history, Germany is cautious about national symbols, and Nationalismus has a strongly negative ring. Many Germans distinguish it from Patriotismus or even Verfassungspatriotismus (loyalty to the constitution, a term used by Jürgen Habermas). The 2006 home World Cup, das Sommermärchen, made waving flags more relaxed. Der Nationalist is a nationalist. It has no plural."
